     "text": "========================================================================================\n           60-SECOND RAPID-FIRE GATE PROBLEM DIAGNOSTIC FLOWCHART\n========================================================================================\n\nSTART: Problem Inspection\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba QUESTION TYPE 1: Signal Classification & Energy / Power\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Is the signal finite duration & square integrable (e.g., pulses, e^(-at)u(t))?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba YES: ENERGY SIGNAL \u2500\u2500\u25ba E = \u222b|x|\u00b2 dt \u2208 (0, \u221e), Power P = 0.\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Is the signal periodic or an undamped complex phasor (e^(j\u03c9t), cos(\u03c9t))?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba YES: POWER SIGNAL \u2500\u2500\u25ba P = (1/T\u2080) \u222b_{T\u2080} |x|\u00b2 dt \u2208 (0, \u221e), Energy E = \u221e.\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Is the signal growing (t u(t), e^(at)u(t)) or inverse root (1/\u221at)?\n  \u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba YES: NENP SIGNAL \u2500\u2500\u25ba Neither Energy nor Power!\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba QUESTION TYPE 2: Continuous-Time Periodicity (Sum of Signals)\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Compute individual periods T\u2081, T\u2082, ...\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Form ratio T\u2081 / T\u2082:\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Is T\u2081 / T\u2082 IRRATIONAL (e.g. contains unmatched \u03c0)?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba STOP: Signal is STRICTLY APERIODIC!\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Is T\u2081 / T\u2082 RATIONAL (a/b)?\n  \u2502     \u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba PERIODIC! \u2500\u2500\u25ba T\u2080 = LCM(T\u2081, T\u2082) = LCM(a, c) / HCF(b, d).\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Modulus involved? Check DC offset: If |A| < |B|, period DOES NOT halve!\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba QUESTION TYPE 3: Discrete-Time Periodicity\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Compute ratio R = \u03a9\u2080 / (2\u03c0).\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Does R contain \u03c0 (irrational, e.g. 2 / (2\u03c0) = 1/\u03c0)?\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba STOP: Sequence is STRICTLY APERIODIC!\n  \u2502     \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Is R a rational fraction m / N\u2080 in lowest terms?\n  \u2502     \u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba PERIODIC! \u2500\u2500\u25ba Fundamental Period N\u2080 = denominator samples!\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Discrete Decimation y[n] = x[Mn]? \u2500\u2500\u25ba N_new = N\u2080 / gcd(N\u2080, M).\n  \u2502\n  \u251c\u2500\u25ba QUESTION TYPE 4: Singularity Function & Delta Calculus\n  \u2502     \u2502\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Linear argument \u03b4(at \u00b1 b)? \u2500\u2500\u25ba (1/|a|) \u03b4(t \u00b1 b/a). (If discrete: \u03b4[an] = \u03b4[n]!)\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Nonlinear argument \u03b4(g(t))? \u2500\u2500\u25ba Find roots g(t\u1d62) = 0, sum \u03b4(t - t\u1d62) / |g'(t\u1d62)|.\n  \u2502     \u251c\u2500\u25ba Sifting with derivative: \u222b x(t) \u03b4'(t - t\u2080) dt? \u2500\u2500\u25ba Result is strictly -x'(t\u2080)!\n  \u2502     \u2514\u2500\u25ba Monomial product: t \u00b7 \u03b4'(t)? \u2500\u2500\u25ba Result is strictly -\u03b4(t)!\n  \u2502\n  \u2514\u2500\u25ba QUESTION TYPE 5: Time Transformation y(t) = x(at \u00b1 b)\n        \u2502\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba Do NOT shift and scale graphs mentally!\n              Use the Point-Mapping Formula:\n                          t_new = (t_old \u2213 b) / a\n              Transform vertices, plot, and connect!\n========================================================================================"
